Start the legacy display probe after the root volume is secured.

``native_legacy_display_late_probe()``'s first act, after the five
non-blocking probes, is a five-second ``waitForMatchingService`` for the
``IOCoreSurfaceRoot`` name -- and that name is published by
``IOSurfaceRoot::start()``, which ``bsd_init()`` reaches only after
``bsd_autoconf()`` has returned and ``vfs_mountroot()`` has run.  The call
used to sit at the end of ``bsd_autoconf()``, so the wait blocked the very
boot that would publish what it was waiting for.

Measured on the QEMU target (21H461):

  * the early probe retains the display object at guest t~17.2 s (stage 3),
  * the late probe runs at t~27.8 s,
  * its five-second wait closes at t~32.8 s with the service absent,
  * ``IOSurfaceRoot::installMemoryRegions()`` lands at t~51.8 s.

So raising the timeout cannot help: it deadlocks.  Moving the call past
``IOSecureBSDRoot()`` puts it where the root volume is known to be up, and
the wait then returns at once because the service is already published.

The five non-blocking probes that ran before the wait -- keystore, HID,
VirtIO input, shared window, QemuMetal -- move with it.  None of them is
needed to mount the root volume, and all of them still run before launchd,
so SpringBoard sees the same devices it saw before, marginally later.

--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1013,6 +1013,21 @@
 	}
 
 	IOSecureBSDRoot(rootdevice);
+#if (DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG) && defined(XNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY) && XNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY
+	/* The original IOSurface personality requires the genuine IOBSD resource,
+	 * and the default-off framebuffer instrument may start only after that
+	 * resource is published -- which IOKitBSDInit() does.  Waiting here used
+	 * to block the boot: IOSurfaceRoot publishes "IOCoreSurfaceRoot" only
+	 * once the root volume is mounted, and bsd_init() reaches mountroot only
+	 * after bsd_autoconf() returns, so a five-second wait in bsd_autoconf()
+	 * waited on the very boot it was blocking.  Measured on the QEMU target:
+	 * the wait closed at t~32.8 s with the service absent and
+	 * IOSurfaceRoot::installMemoryRegions() landed at t~51.8 s.  So the call
+	 * moved here, past IOSecureBSDRoot(): the point where the root volume is
+	 * known to be up and the service is therefore already published. */
+	extern void native_legacy_display_late_probe(void);
+	native_legacy_display_late_probe();
+#endif
 
 	mountlist.tqh_first->mnt_flag |= MNT_ROOTFS;
 
